# Runtime state (per-machine, created by the app)
favorites.json
session-names.json
session-mcp.json
ui-skill-runs.json
ui-skill-schedules.json
skill-favorites.json
prompts.json
prompt-history.json
spend-cache.json
bedrock-models.json
corrections.json
projects.json
session-projects.json
# The folded transcript corpus (lib/corpus.js). It normally lives under %LOCALAPPDATA%\claude-code-ui
# precisely so it stays OUT of this checkout — but CLAUDE_UI_DATA_DIR can point here, and an untracked
# file in the checkout makes `git status --porcelain` dirty, which makes POST /api/version/pull answer
# 409 `dirty-main`: the panel would permanently block its own Update button.
transcript-cache.json
# The API token (N9) lives under %LOCALAPPDATA%\claude-code-ui for the same reason as the line above AND a
# second one: it is a SECRET, and `DATA_DIR === ROOT` in production means the checkout. This rule is the
# belt for the CLAUDE_UI_DATA_DIR case — a token that reaches a commit is a token that has to be rotated.
api-token
# core.js writeJsonAtomic writes `<file>.<pid>.<ms>.tmp` next to its target, so without this rule every
# atomic write of a store in this directory would flap that same dirty flag.
*.tmp

# Dependencies (none today — pure Node — but future-proof)
node_modules/

# Logs / OS cruft
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
ui-prefs.json

# the throwaway test runner (wraps makeSandbox) — scratch, never committed
.tmp-run-tests.js
# …and the throwaway mutation harnesses. Untracked in the checkout they make `git status --porcelain` dirty,
# and POST /api/version/pull then answers 409 `dirty-main`; tracked, they would ship to main.
.tmp-mutate*.js
